---

<ProjectLayout {...page}>
    <p>Individual final project, 4.105 Geometric Disciplines and Architecture Skills, MIT Master of Architecture</p>
    <p>Instructor: <a href="https://architecture.mit.edu/people/j-jih">J. Jih</a></p>
    <p>Source code on <a href="https://github.com/xdd44-utopia/MITGeometricDisciplines">GitHub</a></p>
    <p>The major part of this project mainly investigates and integrates two geometrical techniques: Computationally generated forms with trigonometric functions and arbitrary shape's curved folding of different materials with a certain thickness. Further, the final project aims at creating dynamic transparency through accurate control of parameters including strip and gap width, dynamic radius, and different materials.</p>
